PARITY (web HelpSegment.tsx → native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources: useTranslation only — no fetch. The three "always available" affordances
  (press ? for shortcuts, take a tour, report a bug) are modelled as the surface's
  available-action feed, bound through the shared P1/S8 state-holder (HelpSegmentModel);
  no networking/dispatch lives in the view.
Shared components: maps web @/components/ui to the native P1/S9 component library
  (TSCard, TSButton, TSEmptyState, TSSkeleton, TSFadeIn) + tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS /
  TSSpacing / TSRadius). No Tailwind ports, no raw hex.
Window events → native dispatch seam: the web `window.dispatchEvent('toggle-keyboard-
  shortcuts')`, `dispatchTourLauncherOpen()`, `window.dispatchEvent('open-feedback-modal')`
  become ClosureHelpActionDispatcher(onShortcuts/onTour/onFeedback), routed by HelpActionKind.
iconOnly prop → HelpSegmentPresentation (.expanded shows keycap + labels; .iconOnly shows
  icons with the label carried by tooltip/VoiceOver).
i18n keys (all 7 from source, resolved through the P1/S10 facade — no English literals in
  Swift): shortcuts.tooltip, shortcuts.openAria, shortcuts.hintSuffix, tour.launcher.openShort,
  tour.launcher.openAria, feedback.openShort, feedback.openAria.
States (every one renders): loading (skeleton pills), empty (friendly card, never blank),
  error (QueryError peer + retry), data (3 affordance buttons), stale/offline (freshness chip
  + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
Accessibility: each button carries the web aria-label as the VoiceOver label, the tooltip as
  the hint + macOS .help(), .isButton trait, focus ring, and the web data-testid/data-tour
  hooks as accessibilityIdentifier (status-bar-feedback-trigger, status-bar-tour-trigger,
  status-bar-keyboard-hint). Keycap is decorative (accessibilityHidden). Reduce-motion is
  honoured by the shared TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton.
Telemetry: HelpSegmentModel.start() emits view.opened surface="HelpSegment" exactly once
  (P1/S11 diagnostics contract), idempotent across appear/disappear.

